{
 "name": "Territorial Kavu — domain P/T kept beside a modal attack trigger",
 "notes": "Kavu's domain characteristic-defining ability had no oracle position, so the mode tagger guessed it into a mode of the 'Whenever this creature attacks, choose one —' trigger by its words, and the Orzhov Pontiff rule (a triggered ability's modes wait for the ability) then deleted it: Kavu had no effects at all. A characteristic-defining ability is now never a mode on a permanent (CR 604.3). Plains, Island, Swamp and Breeding Pool (Forest Island) make four basic land types: Kavu is 4/4. Memory: project_territorial_kavu_cda_never_a_mode_2026-10-14.",
 "recipe": {
  "steps": [
